.TH DEPENGINE 1 "2026-07-10" "depengine" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
depengine \- distro-agnostic dependency installation engine guided by schema.toml
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B depengine
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
depengine is a single-binary dependency installer written in Go.
You describe \fIwhat\fR to install in a declarative
.BR schema.toml ;
the engine decides \fIhow\fR to install each tool by trying methods in
order (native, cargo, go, pip, git, http, ...) until one succeeds,
respecting per-distro conditions, inter-tool dependencies, and
post-installation hooks. The binary is static with no runtime
dependencies on the target machine.
.PP
Checksums resolved via \fB:auto\fR are pinned in \fBschema.lock\fR
for reproducibility. Supported algorithms: SHA-256, SHA-512, SHA-1, MD5.
GPG signature verification is supported via \fBsignature_url\fR
and \fBsigning_key\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install " [flags]"
Installs all tools from the schema, respecting
.BR method_order ,
.BR when ,
.BR requires ,
and topological ordering. See OPTIONS below for flags.
.TP
.B init " [flags]"
Initializes a new depengine project by creating a minimal
.B depengine.toml
or
.B schema.toml
scaffold in the current directory. Use
.B \-\-schema
to specify a custom path.
.TP
.B validate " [flags]"
Validates the schema structure and optionally the system environment.
Reports unknown methods, unknown placeholders, and missing tools.
.TP
.B check " <tool>"
Checks whether a specific tool is installed on the machine. Exits 0
if installed, 1 if not found.
.TP
.B status " [flags]"
Shows the installation status of tools by comparing the state file
against the schema. Reports installed, missing, orphaned, and
outdated tools.
.TP
.B remove " <tool> | --all"
Removes a tool using the adapter that originally installed it. Use
.B --all
to remove every tracked tool.
.TP
.B forget " <tool>"
Removes a tool from the state file without touching the system. Useful
when a tool was removed manually or the state is out of sync.
.TP
.B version
Prints the version and a short description.
.TP
.B completion " bash|zsh|fish"
Prints the shell completion script for the given shell. Source the
output in your shell rc file (e.g.
.BR "source <(depengine completion bash)" )
to enable tab completion.
.TP
.B undo " [flags]"
Reverts the last
.B install
by restoring the previous state snapshot and removing tools that were
added since that snapshot.
.TP
.B sbom " [flags]"
Exports the current depengine state as a Software Bill of Materials (SBOM)
in CycloneDX 1.5 or SPDX 2.3 JSON format. Each installed tool becomes a
component/package in the BOM. Use
.B \-\-format spdx
to switch to SPDX output. Useful for integration with vulnerability scanners
such as grype or trivy.
.TP
.B update " [flags]"
Updates all tools from locked schema versions (git refs, http URLs
with {latest}). Requires a lockfile (\fBschema.lock\fR) generated by a
previous successful \fBinstall\fR. Use
.B \-\-frozen\-lockfile
to abort if the lockfile does not exist.
.TP
.B why " <tool>"
Explains how a tool would be installed: for each method, reports the
status (\fBalready_installed\fR, \fBwould_install\fR,
\fBskip_unavailable\fR, \fBskip_when\fR). Supports \fB--json\fR for
programmatic consumption.
.TP
.B graph " [flags]"
Outputs the dependency graph in one of three formats: Mermaid (flowchart),
DOT (Graphviz), or text (level groups). Use
.B \-\-only
to focus on a single tool and its transitive dependencies.
.TP
.B diff " [flags] [file1] [file2]"
Compares depengine state files between machines or arbitrary paths.
If no files are given, compares the current state with the file specified by
.BR \-\-other .
If one file is given, compares the current state with that file.
If two files are given, compares the two files directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "install flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-schema " <path>"
Path to the schema file. Default: \fBschema.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be installed without executing anything.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose " | \fB\-v\fR"
Detailed per-tool output.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit JSON output for programmatic consumption.
.TP
.BR \-\-only " <tool>"
Install only the specified tool.
.TP
.BR \-\-skip " <tools>"
Skip specific tools (comma-separated list).
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " <tag>"
Only install tools that have the given tag or no tags (e.g. \fB--profile=desktop\fR).
Useful for targeting different machine profiles from a single schema file.
.TP
.BR \-\-sort\-by " <field>"
Sort output by: \fBname\fR, \fBstatus\fR, or \fBmethod\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " <level>"
Log level: \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, or \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-diagnose
Diagnostic mode: implies \fB--dry-run\fR, \fB--verbose\fR, and
\fBdebug\fR log level.
.TP
.BR \-\-jobs " <n>"
Maximum concurrent installations within a topological level. Default: 1
(sequential).
.IP
Warning: Running multiple native package manager installs concurrently may
cause lock contention or corruption. Prefer \fB--jobs=1\fR when installing
many native tools.
.TP
.BR \-\-allow-arbitrary-code
Suppress security warnings for build scripts (arbitrary code execution).
.SS "validate flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-schema " <path>"
Path to the schema file. Default: \fBschema.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-env
Check whether required tools are available in the environment (PATH).
.TP
.BR \-\-format " <fmt>"
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-strict
Treat warnings as errors (exit code 1).
.SS "status flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-schema " <path>"
Override the schema path (default: from state file).
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit JSON output.
.TP
.BR \-\-orphans
Show only orphaned tools (installed but no longer in schema).
.SS "remove flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-all
Remove all tracked tools.
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be removed without executing.
.SS "flags do graph"
.TP
.BR \-\-schema " <path>"
Caminho para o arquivo de schema. Padrão: \fBschema.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " <fmt>"
Formato de saída: \fBmermaid\fR, \fBdot\fR ou \fBtext\fR (padrão).
.TP
.BR \-\-only " <tool>"
Mostra apenas o subgrafo da ferramenta especificada e suas dependências
transitivas.
.TP
.BR \-\-skip " <tools>"
Pula ferramentas específicas (lista separada por vírgulas).
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " <tag>"
Mostra apenas ferramentas com a tag especificada (ex: \fB--profile=server\fR).
.SS "undo flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-list
List available snapshots with timestamps and tool counts.
.TP
.BR \-\-snapshot " <path>"
Restore a specific snapshot file instead of the most recent one.
.SS "sbom flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-format " <fmt>"
Output format: \fBcyclonedx\fR (default) or \fBspdx\fR.
.SS "diff flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output differences as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-other " <path>"
Path to the other state file to compare (used when no arguments are provided).
.SS "why flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Emit JSON output for programmatic consumption.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " <fmt>"
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
.SS "update flags"
.TP
.BR \-\-frozen\-lockfile
Abort if no lockfile exists (prevents resolving {latest} from network).
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be updated without executing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS "Build and validate"
.EX
go build -o depengine .
./depengine validate
.EE
.SS "Validate with environment check and JSON output"
.EX
./depengine validate --check-env --format=json
.EE
.SS "Install all tools from a custom schema"
.EX
./depengine install --schema my-tools.toml
.EE
.SS "Install a single tool verbosely"
.EX
./depengine install --only nvim --verbose
.EE
.SS "Dry run with sorted output"
.EX
./depengine install --dry-run --sort-by name
.EE
.SS "Diagnose: DEBUG + dry-run + verbose"
.EX
./depengine install --diagnose
.EE
.SS "Install with profile (desktop-only)"
.EX
./depengine install --profile=desktop
.EE
.SS "Check if a tool is installed"
.EX
./depengine check nvim
.EE
.SS "Show installation status"
.EX
./depengine status
./depengine status --json
./depengine status --orphans
.EE
.SS "Remove a tool"
.EX
./depengine remove bat
./depengine remove --all --dry-run
.EE
.SS "Enable shell completion"
.EX
# Bash
source <(depengine completion bash)

# Zsh
source <(depengine completion zsh)
.SS "Show dependency graph"
.EX
./depengine graph
./depengine graph --format=mermaid
./depengine graph --format=dot --only=tool_name
./depengine graph --profile=desktop
.EE
.SS "Export SBOM"
.EX
./depengine sbom
./depengine sbom --format=spdx
.EE
.SS "Compare state files (diff)"
.EX
# Compare current state with --other file
./depengine diff --other machine2.json

# Compare current state with file
./depengine diff machine2.json

# Compare two files directly
./depengine diff state1.json state2.json

# Output as JSON
./depengine diff --json machine2.json
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_DETECT_SCRIPT
Caminho para o script
.B detect_os.sh
O padrão é: primeiro procura na pasta \fBscripts/\fR junto ao
binário, depois no \fBPATH\fR.
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_TRACE_ID
Trace ID propagated to subprocesses for correlated logging.
.TP
.B DEPENGINE_LOG_JSON
Set to \fB1\fR to enable JSON output for the structured logger.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for the state file. The state file is stored at
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/depengine/state.json\fR, falling back to
\fB~/.local/state/depengine/state.json\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B schema.toml
The declarative schema describing tools and installation methods.
Shipped with the project as a reference template.
.TP
.B scripts/detect_os.sh
System detection script invoked at runtime to gather OS, architecture,
distro, libc, and init-system facts.
.TP
.BI $XDG_STATE_HOME/depengine/state.json
State file tracking which tools were installed, by which method, and
when. Used by the
.B status
and
.B remove
commands.
.TP
.B scripts/depengine-completion.bash
.B scripts/depengine-completion.zsh
.B scripts/depengine-completion.fish
Shell completion scripts emitted by the
.B completion
command.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
0
Success — all tools installed or already present.
.TP
1
Some tool failed to install, or strict-mode validation found warnings.
.TP
2
Schema error — invalid TOML, validation failure, unknown method, or
unknown placeholder.
.TP
3
Runtime error —
.B detect_os.sh
not found, state I/O failure, or other infrastructure error.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
The project README and
.B docs/cheatsheet.md
contain the complete
.B schema.toml
reference, method examples, and placeholder documentation.
